A lone ':' as a statement, a ':' with a space before a keyword name, and
a ':' at end of file. The validator must report each without panicking,
and the formatter must not glue the colon onto a neighboring token.
Suspected issue: no diagnostic for ':;', ': IF nCount > 0;' or a trailing ':' (only the then-unmatched :ENDIF is reported); unexpected_token says it flags the first token a statement cannot accept, and a lone ':' can begin no SSL statement.
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE nCount;
:;
nCount := 1;
: IF nCount > 0;
nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;
:
-- format --
:DECLARE nCount;
:;
nCount := 1;
: IF nCount > 0;
nCount += 1;
:ENDIF;
:
-- diagnostics --
6:1-6:7 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:1-6:7 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
